      'Turn-flow example: After dealing, players may pass or pick the blind depending on table rules. The picker takes the blind, buries cards, and usually forms a hidden partnership (for example called-ace or jack-of-diamonds variants). Play is clockwise in tricks with mandatory suit following. Trump order is fixed with queens and jacks highest, plus diamonds as trumps in common five-player rules. After all tricks, card points determine whether picker side or defenders win.',
